<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_BreaklightCondition.xml            UtinniPatches · GREENTIDE_MECHANICS_2 M5
  ============================================================================
  greentide_kit_spec.md "M5. Breaklight — clarity as the disaster": "reuse
  ruled RM_GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather as a rare IncidentDef-triggered
  condition preset: forces RUT_BreaklightClear WeatherDef (clear, harsh
  palette), tempOffset +12 C (INVENTED — stacks on the ~45 C ambient into
  vanilla heatstroke territory via the untouched HediffGiver_Heat), duration
  3-8 hours (INVENTED)." Duration itself lives on the firing IncidentDef
  (Defs/IncidentDefs/RUT_Breaklight.xml durationDays), consumed by
  IncidentWorker_MakeGameCondition.TryExecuteWorker exactly the way
  RUT_GradientSurge.xml's own header already documents — not repeated here.

  conditionClass = RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather
  (ALPHA_MECHANICS_KIT_1, ruled and already shipped). tempOffset IS a real,
  already-shipped EnvironmentalWeatherExtension field (verified against
  Source/EnvironmentalWeatherExtension.cs this pass, not guessed) — read by
  GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather.TemperatureOffset() and faded in/out via
  GameConditionUtility.LerpInOutValue over temperatureTransitionTicks, tuned
  below to 2500 (INVENTED, this pass's own — a faster ramp than the
  extension's own 5000 default, matching "temperatures spike" rather than a
  slow drift; proportionally still a small fraction of even the shortest
  3-hour duration).

  Two modExtensions, same "a Def can carry more than one, filtered by type"
  shape RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock and others already rely on:
    - EnvironmentalWeatherExtension: the ruled condition's own config
      (forcedWeather + tempOffset), no damage/hediff/rot/density fields set.
    - RM_GlowMultiplierOverrideExtension (this item's own M5 build, new
      class): read directly by BiomeGlowPatches.CurCelestialSunGlow_Postfix,
      NOT by GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather — glowMultiplier 1.0
      (explicit, matching the class default) undoes the Greentide's own
      permanent 0.75 BiomeGlowMultiplierExtension for the condition's
      duration, "the steam deflects the sun" mechanism switched fully off
      rather than merely dimmed less.

  allowUnderground=false (unlike the Roil lock's own true): Breaklight is a
  sun event — a cave/underground map has no sun to snap clear, and the ~45 C
  ambient/dry-heat framing this condition prices in is a surface story. Same
  choice RUT_GradientSurge.xml already made for its own (different reason,
  same field) tidal event.

  canBePermanent left unset/false: fired only via RUT_Breaklight.xml's
  IncidentDef, same posture RUT_GradientSurge.xml already documents for its
  own incident-fired condition.

  MayRequire is load-bearing: conditionClass and both modExtension classes
  live in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards; forcedWeather (RUT_BreaklightClear)
  carries no MayRequire of its own (plain-vanilla-field WeatherDef, no
  cross-mod class reference) so no extra gate is needed for it specifically.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_BreaklightCondition</defName>
    <conditionClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather</conditionClass>
    <label>Breaklight</label>
    <description>The Roil has lifted. The Greentide stands under a bare, merciless sun, and every degree of the heat it was hiding is suddenly real.</description>
    <startMessage>The standing fog tears open all at once — Breaklight has come, and the sun over the Greentide is bare and full.</startMessage>
    <endMessage>The Roil closes back over the canopy. Breaklight has passed.</endMessage>
    <letterText>The fog blanket has lifted without warning. For the next several hours the Greentide stands under a cloudless, merciless sun — full accuracy, full heat, and every wild thing in sight running for shade.</letterText>
    <allowUnderground>false</allowUnderground>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.EnvironmentalWeatherExtension">
        <forcedWeather>RUT_BreaklightClear</forcedWeather>
        <tempOffset>12</tempOffset>
        <temperatureTransitionTicks>2500</temperatureTransitionTicks>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GlowMultiplierOverrideExtension">
        <glowMultiplier>1.0</glowMultiplier>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
